From 0d92d81f6587db0ac3c779745863f6db401a9726 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:29:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0308 -- script VM: LITTOREG builds its
 literal in the register

WHY: LITTOREG (the "movl" opcode) is the second most frequent VM instruction in old verb-template
scripts: 722 a tick on Maniac Mansion Deluxe. It built its value in the address-taken codeOp.Args[1]
(SetInt32, then FixupArgument), then copied the 20-byte RuntimeScriptValue into the register. Building
it in the register directly removes that round trip. Read from the build's own -S: movl's path is
shorter by 6/4/5/3/5 instructions for no-fixup/gdata/func/string/import literals, ~4.1k instructions
a tick on MMD's mix (LAB-MMD.md 18.7, 19).

WHAT: reg1.SetInt32(arg2); FixupArgument(reg1, ...) in place of the codeOp.Args[1] build and copy.
Exact: FixupArgument reads only the code word, the fixup tables, the strings and the stack, never the
registers, and in every case either leaves the value as SetInt32 made it or overwrites it whole, so the
register ends with the same five fields. ASSERT_CC_ERROR is empty in release builds. In a
DEBUG_CC_EXEC build it would return after the register was written rather than before, on an
error-abort path only. WRITELIT is unchanged. __DJGPP__-gated.

-S check: Run 3,365 -> 3,395 instructions; `this` reloads unchanged (70); the loop head, back-edge and
every other hot handler identical.

Measured at fixed 40000 cycles on MMD's character select: script event 9.354 -> 9.257 ms/tick (-0.097;
band -0.07 to -0.13). Determinism guard (state digests every 25 ticks, script events, AutoPilot log,
PH*.BMP) EQUAL on MMD, AGS Quest and 5 Days (seeded), with baseline-twice and perturbation controls;
screen gate pixel-equal at every freeze tick (LAB-MMD.md 19, 19.1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
---
 Engine/script/cc_instance.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/script/cc_instance.cpp b/Engine/script/cc_instance.cpp
index c2cb3d44d..a9bb5f607 100644
--- a/Engine/script/cc_instance.cpp
+++ b/Engine/script/cc_instance.cpp
@@ -838,11 +838,21 @@ ccInstError ccInstance::Run(int32_t curpc)
         case SCMD_LITTOREG:
         {
             auto &reg1 = _registers[op_arg1];
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+            // DOS-PORT patch 0308: build the literal and apply its fixup IN the register, not in
+            // codeOp.Args[1] followed by a 20-byte copy into it. FixupArgument reads only the code
+            // word, the fixup tables and the stack, never the registers, and sets the value's
+            // fields exactly as before; so the register ends up with the same five fields.
+            reg1.SetInt32(op_arg2);
+            FixupArgument(reg1, codeInst->_code_fixups[_pc + 2], codeInst->_code[_pc + 2], _stackBegin, codeInst->_strings);
+            ASSERT_CC_ERROR();
+#else
             codeOp.Args[1].SetInt32(op_arg2); // patch 0293/0295: the whole value, before its fixup
             FixupArgument(codeOp.Args[1], codeInst->_code_fixups[_pc + 2], codeInst->_code[_pc + 2], _stackBegin, codeInst->_strings);
             ASSERT_CC_ERROR();
             const auto &arg_value = codeOp.Arg2();
             reg1 = arg_value;
+#endif
             break;
         }
         case SCMD_MEMREAD:
